<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dubai Creek</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dubai <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a> is a saltwater inlet that divides Dubai into Deira and Bur Dubai. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-bu-falasah">Al Bu Falasah</a> settled on its banks in 1833, and its sheltered harbour made Dubai a centre of pearling and trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Its dredging in 1959–1961 under Sheikh Rashid bin Saeed allowed larger ships to enter and launched Dubai's growth as a port.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dubai-creek.jpg" alt="Dubai Creek" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Phil6007 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_view_of_Dubai_Creek.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
